    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d354">

                <pb facs="0455" n="375" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg375"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/400: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-11-29T13:00:00-05:45">November 29, 1930—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>163. Your telegram number 134, November 26, 2 p.m.<anchor n="99" xml:id="d354-f1"
                    /> When I communicated to the Minister for Foreign Affairs this morning
                    (President Moncada being out of town) the information summarized in my 158,
                    November 22, 11 a.m., he expressed his gratefulness and said that he believed
                    the boundary protocol would be signed before <pb facs="0456" n="376"
                        xml:id="pg376"/> the end of this year and hoped that after seeing President
                    Moncada he would be able to fix a date on which to base further
                    arrangements.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
